claude: true
prompt: >
  You are working on locale-simple, one codebase that publishes six packages
  (Perl on CPAN, Python, JavaScript, PHP, Go and Rust) with the same gettext
  API. Read .claude/rules/locale-simple-rules.md, then pick the
  highest-priority actionable ticket from the karr board (`karr board`), claim
  it, and complete it through the agent whose lane covers it (the lane table is
  in that file). A change to one runtime is usually a change to all six — keep
  the siblings in step. Verify with `prove -lr t/`, `python python/test.py`,
  `cd js && npm install && npm test`, `composer test`, `go test ./go/...` and
  `cargo test --manifest-path rust/Cargo.toml`; the `-l` is mandatory, without
  it the installed CPAN release is loaded instead of lib/. dist.ini is the
  build truth; cpanfile and Changes follow it. Never run `dzil release`, never
  tag, never push commits, never upload to CPAN, PyPI, npm or crates.io.
